{
  "abstract": "For every finite simple graph whose graph and delta complement have no isolated vertices, the sum of their total-domination numbers is at most the number of vertices plus twice the number of distinct vertex degrees of the original graph. This is Conjecture 4 of Pinhe Chen.",
